{"records":[{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s3jtdhjdbs","title":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Protein import motor complex reacts to mitochondrial misfolding by reducing protein import and activating mitophagy'","description":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Mitochondrial import loss induces mitophagy without membrane depolarization'. We hypothesized that inhibition of mitochondrial protein import induced mitophagy independent of mitochondrial depolarization. This dataset contains raw Illumina sequencing data for all samples from a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen for mitophagy regulators. The genome-wide library is Brunello from Doench et al Nat Biotechnol. 2016. We found that the pre-sequence translocase-associated motor complex PAM controls mitophagy induction. Loss of PAM caused a loss in protein import and was sufficient to induce mitophagy without depolarization.\nThe samples have been sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 in single end mode with 75+8 cycles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-05T15:38:53.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s3jtdhjdbs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s3jtdhjdbs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Michaelis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Melinda","last_name":"Brunstein","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Süleyman","last_name":"Bozkurt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ludovico","last_name":"Alves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Wegner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manuel","last_name":"Kaulich","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Pohl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Münch","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Mitochondrion","Mitophagy","Genetic Screening","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hx4nwr8yyd","title":"Data for: Therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia developing 14 years after allogeneic stem cell transplantation, from a persistent R882H-DNMT3A mutated clone of patient origin.","description":"Supplementary (DOCX  2.34MB): \nMaterials and methods. \nFig. S1. TP53 mutation found in the lung carcinoma cells taken from the patient in 2012. \nFig. S2. Karyotype illustrating the metaphases of the 2015 therapy-related myelodysplastic syndrome cells. \nFig. S3. Paint of chromosome 15 (green) by fluorescent in situ hybridization. \nFig. S4. Analysis of the chimerism (Mentype® Chimera® software, Biotype) at 2015 therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis. \nFig. S5. IDH1, DNMT3A and NPM1 mutations found at the time of the acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis in 2001. \nFig. S6. DNMT3A and TP53 mutations found at the time of the therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis in 2015. \nFig. S7. Standard curve for the ASO-qPCR. \nFig. S8. Sensitivity assay for quantitative ASO-qPCR. \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-07-18T12:28:12.179Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hx4nwr8yyd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hx4nwr8yyd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Iván","last_name":"Martín","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Felipe J","last_name":"Chaves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rosario","last_name":"Abellán","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Francisca","last_name":"García","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mar","last_name":"Tormo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Carlos","last_name":"Solano","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Juan-Carlos","last_name":"Hernandez-Boluda","orcid":null},{"first_name":"María Dolores","last_name":"Olivares","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Eva","last_name":"Villamón","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Fernando","last_name":"Domingo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Blanca","last_name":"Navarro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marisa","last_name":"Calabuig","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Paula","last_name":"Amat","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alicia","last_name":"Serrano","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Cytogenetics"],"journal_issn":["00144800"]},{"id":"nnxh5d35nd","title":"Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 screen identified KLF11 as a druggable suppressor for sarcoma cancer stem cells","description":"The original, unprocessed data alongside the paper","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-05-31T01:39:45.722Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nnxh5d35nd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nnxh5d35nd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Le","last_name":"Qu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zhpg8xshp9","title":"Lawrence et al., PNAS 2026","description":"Data from “Lawrence et al., 2026 A Genome-Wide Screen Identifies that PLCG2 Restrains Lysosomal GCase Activity.\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-22T18:23:16.389Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zhpg8xshp9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zhpg8xshp9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Baris","last_name":"Bingol","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Natural Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":139065,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":178,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":139065,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":138332,"restricted":69,"embargoed":664},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2300},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1386},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":660},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":473},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":450},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":435},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico","count":421},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":386},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":328},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":275}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"